# CODEOWNERS: who must review changes to which paths.
#
# Each line is a path pattern (gitignore syntax) followed by one or more owners.
# The LAST matching line wins, so put the general rule first and the
# specific ones after it.
#
# What it does today (solo repo): GitHub requests a review from the owner on
# every PR that touches a matching path.
# What it does in a team: with "Require review from Code Owners" enabled in
# branch protection, a PR cannot merge until an owner of every touched path
# approves. You cannot approve your own PR, which is why
# scripts/branch-protection.sh leaves that option off until a second person
# joins the repo.

# Default owner for everything
*                       @hamza-tleiss

# The delivery pipeline itself. A change here can publish images or deploy
# to production, so in a team this is where a platform owner is listed.
/.github/               @hamza-tleiss
/scripts/               @hamza-tleiss

# Container build definitions
/api/Dockerfile         @hamza-tleiss
/frontend/Dockerfile    @hamza-tleiss
/frontend/nginx.conf    @hamza-tleiss
/compose.yaml           @hamza-tleiss

# Infrastructure (Module 4 onward)
/infra/                 @hamza-tleiss
/deploy/                @hamza-tleiss
